00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:00.950 align:start position:0%
 
okay  so now that you've had some time to sit  with it how are you feeling about being  evicted  oh i feel great  [Laughter]  honestly i i do i feel great i'm just  happy that i had this experience and  i'm i'm not in the big brother house  anymore  it's bittersweet  um  you know julie showed you the alliance  who formed who was  once who essentially got you out  obviously they were able to get others  to flip the vote um was there someone or  something about that alliance that  surprised you or surprised you the most  not at all i put two and two together  early in the week and i  i knew that there was something else  cooking up and i i know that you know  michael definitely tried to look out for  me and he tried to drop hints and i just  wasn't picking them up  um  looking back on it do you  wish that you guys hadn't used the veto  or do you still feel like it was a move  worth making  i'm 50 50 on that you know big risk big  reward but at the same time  if there was any point that i could have  believed anything that was coming out of  monty's mouth  i would have definitely been trying to  convince daniel not to use the power of  veto  it's hard it's like a big brother  everyone lies but then it's like when  someone's telling you like don't do it  you're like but you want me to do it so  right exactly  it's hard um you know obviously we saw  um julie mention it and we you know  uh turner kind of hinted at it at his  speech a couple weeks ago  um that there's been sort of  mistreatment and bullying of taylor i  mean i sort of want to get your thoughts  on that and if you have any sort of  regrets about how  uh you treated taylor  um  i definitely do regret how i treated  taylor i think that i um  had a hand in giving her the short end  of the stick and i wish that i could go  back but you know i  take full ownership of things that were  said and done and i look forward to  looking back on all of it and being able  to  um sit with taylor and really go over  all those things and moving forward  hopefully we have a beautiful friendship  and that we can really work and i can  learn from a lot of what happened  yeah that was my next question was if  you had plans or had a desire to speak  with taylor after everything  absolutely um you know we've  i told her i loved her before i left and  i truly mean that we were holding hands  in the nomination chair before i was  evicted  um  you know those are those are true  feelings and  i i want to be better moving forward and  i want to be better with her moving  forward so yeah  do you feel like sort of how you know  julia mentioned it in her speech or  sorry in her interview with you that um  you know this alliance sort of formed  after the whole big fight with daniel  and all of that kind of stuff do you  feel like sort of how things went down  with taylor is why not the only reason  obviously but part of the reason you got  evicted  yes  yeah what other reasons do you think was  it uh that you think that you ended up  on the outside of that house  um i thought that i can control and  manipulate somebody else's game and i  put taylor i picked taylor as my festy  bestie because i thought i could use her  as a shield and  i was going by the words of my alliance  members and saying that she's the target  and that's what it comes down to is that  i was trying to advance my game so  strategically i figured  bringing her as close as i could to me  that that would make that happen  um what surprised you the most about  playing big brother  i mean  it's exhausting  campaigning for yourself and trying to  trying to promise things to people that  you know you can't promise anything to  any of these people um  but  the  the mental exhaustion is is real and  you  i wasn't  expecting what the totality of that was  going to be  at what point um  did you realize that you were  probably like  most definitely going home i mean did  you think even towards the end that  there was a chance or did you kind of  accept it by the time you were sitting  on the eviction block  i  i accepted it the moment i was sitting  on the block but i knew that i wasn't  going to give up  and i think that that showed through  until  five minutes before i sat in that  nomination chair before the live show  um who do you think um you know  obviously there's still a lot of game  left to be played um and you haven't  obviously watched the stuff but who do  you think is going to go far in this  game based off just the information you  have right now  michael i want michael to win this game  i want michael to go all the way i want  him sitting in that chair and i really  do hope that these  whoever's in the jury that they make  that happen

